SUMMARY:The Notebook
DESCRIPTION:A Love Story for the Ages \nBased on the best-selling novel that inspired the iconic film\, THE NOTEBOOK tells the story of Allie and Noah\, both from different worlds\, who share a lifetime of love despite the forces that threaten to pull them apart. “Full of butterfly-inducing highs and beautiful songs” (Entertainment Weekly)\, THE NOTEBOOK is a deeply moving portrait of the enduring power of love. \nChris Jones of The Chicago Tribune says THE NOTEBOOK is “absolutely gorgeous\, not to be missed\,” and The New York Daily News calls it “a love story for the ages.” \nTHE NOTEBOOK is directed by Michael Grief (Dear Evan Hansen\, Next to Normal\, RENT) and Schele Williams (The Wiz\, Aida)\, and features music and lyrics by multi-platinum singer-songwriter Ingrid Michaelson\, book by Bekah Brunstetter (NBC’s “This Is Us”)\, and choreography by Katie Spelman.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/the-notebook/2026-07-19/1/
LOCATION:DPAC Presented by First Horizon\, 123 Vivian St / William V. "Bill" Bell Way\, Durham\, 27701
CATEGORIES:Live Performance
